 "answers": [
  {
   "question": "Arlanda C (`740000556`): withheld: OSM joins no footway to the platforms and tags no entrance",
   "answer": "Partly answered. The station is underground, directly under SkyCity between Terminals 4 and 5, with one platform and two tracks (Wikipedia). Passengers pass turnstile gates between the station and SkyCity, where the station fee (130 SEK) is checked (AIAB, Swedavia). OSM has the two platform areas, long escalators (w487787886/7), one lift (n4802014315) and three entrance nodes with fee validators. They are just not joined together. The owner is Arlandabanan Infrastructure AB and the station is run by A-Train AB, not Swedavia or Jernhusen.",
   "_source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arlanda_Central_Station; https://arlandabananinfrastructure.se/en/the-railway/about-arlandabanan/; https://www.swedavia.com/arlanda/train/; OSM, read 2026-10-30"
  }
